      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "## A photogrammetric mesh, drawn where it stands\n\nA **3D Tiles** tileset — the AGI headquarters in Exton, Pennsylvania, surveyed from the air — added straight from its URL, with no data source behind it.\n\nTwo things had to change for it to draw at all. A tileset states its geometry at its **real altitude**, and this map's ground is flat at zero, so the mesh floated some 300 m up and vanished from any close or tilted camera: the layer now **brings it down to the ground**. And the camera stopped at 60°, short of the 69.5° this view needs.\n\n**Ctrl + drag** to rotate and tilt. To move the mesh, open the side panel with the arrow at the top left of the map, expand the layer, and look under **Position**.\n\n**Needs internet**: the tiles come from a public bucket, and they are heavy — around 300 MB of GPU memory at close range."
      }
    },
